OL,3,ASyrians struggle with soaring prices as
OL,4,Acrisis challenges post-Assad recovery
OL,5,
OL,6,FLast month, protests erupted in squares
OL,7,Fand streets across Syria. People burned
OL,8,Ftyres, blocked roads and chanted
OL,9,Fslogans, angry at the government's
OL,10,Fdecision to raise fuel prices again. It
OL,11,Fwas the largest show of discontent yet
OL,12,Fsince President Ahmed al-Sharaa came to
OL,13,Fpower two years ago.
OL,15,FSpeaking on a Syrian TV channel, a man
OL,16,Fsaid he still supported the authorities
OL,17,Fbut that his situation had deteriorated
OL,18,Fto the point where he could no longer
OL,19,Fafford to buy bread. "Honestly,"
OL,20,Fanother said, "we have begun to fear
OL,21,Fwhat kind of new decision each morning
OL,22,Fwill bring".
OL,23,APub: 30-OctQpppppppppppppppppppppG14/40
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
